course: dictionary
lesson: 1968
title: Compile: two meanings, one word
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: The word compile has two main meanings. The first is to collect things and put them together, such as a list, a scrapbook or a class report. A class might compile a list of their favourite books.
explain: The second meaning is from computing: to turn the code a programmer writes into a program the computer can run. Rust's compiler does this job. «Rust's compiler is strict, so beginners see long red errors, but they usually explain the problem and often suggest a fix.»
explain: Use the context to find the meaning. «In Rust, a variable cannot change unless it is declared with "mut"; "let x = 5; x = 6;" is a compile error.» The words code and error tell you this is the computing meaning. Check by swapping in your meaning: "is an error when the code fails to become a program" makes sense.
fact: Compile is a verb: I compile, she compiles, we compiled, we are compiling.
fact: Compilation is the noun, for example a compilation of short stories put together in one book.
fact: «Compile a list» means to collect items and put them together in order.
fact: «Compile the code» means to turn written code into a program the computer can run.
fact: «let x = 5; x = 6;» will not compile, because a variable cannot change unless it is declared with "mut", as in «let mut x = 5;».
exercise: Ava wants to compile a list of the ten best books she has read. What does compile mean here? | To delete all the books from the shelf | *To collect things and put them together in one list | To lose the list on the bus | To read every page twice
exercise: «"let x = 5; x = 6;" is a compile error.» What does compile mean here? | To turn the code into a poem | To collect the code into a scrapbook | *To turn code into a program, and this code fails | To read the code out loud
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the tool that turns code into a program. | *compiler | strict | Rust | errors
test: Which word is the noun for a collection of things put together? | compiled | *compilation | compiler | compiling
test: What does "compile the code" mean? | *To turn written code into a program the computer can run | To write a poem about the code | To draw the code on paper | To wait for the computer to start up
exam: Read «In Rust, a variable cannot change unless it is declared with "mut".» Which meaning of compile fits «a compile error», and why? | The school meaning, because a list of errors was put together | The computing meaning, because the programmer read the code aloud | *The computing meaning, because the code fails to become a program | The school meaning, because the errors were collected in a scrapbook
